    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by elite speed and favorable situational matchups. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98) stands as our strongest play of the day, leveraging an elite matchup against a right-handed starter who struggles with pitch delivery times; this environment maximizes his high-upside speed profile, which is critical for our scarcity targets in Stolen Bases. Close behind is **Yordan Alvarez** (77.46), whose elite 0.443 xwOBA and favorable slotting in the #2 hole make him our premier power threat against Johnson. **Trea Turner** (77.28) also garners a Strong rating, benefiting significantly from his top-of-the-order role and a favorable matchup against Martinez, providing the necessary efficiency to push our Roto categories forward.\n\nTactical adjustments highlight our daily philosophy, specifically regarding platoon advantages. **Lars Nootbaar** (65.16) and **Christian Yelich** (68.82) are both high-value starts today, bolstered by dynamic platoon edges against right-handed pitching that lift their scores well above their raw projections. Conversely, **Junior Caminero** (55.73) remains a marginal play; despite his upside, the combination of facing an elite arm like Wheeler and a projected score dip due to SP skill forces him into the UTIL slot, though he remains active to keep our game cap usage efficient. **Caleb Durbin** (42.69) sits at the bottom of our active threshold; the optimizer remains wary of the matchup against Imanaga, whose proficiency against left-handed bats provides a significant hurdle, but his potential for late-game defensive contributions and situational speed keeps him in the lineup over the currently sidelined **Josh Smith**, whose benching is solidified by his absence from the projected starting lineup and significant platoon penalties.",
